  "dependencies": {
    "identical_groups": "f88_top_pale_spread is shared by f88r.6 and the corresponding f88r.5 alternative. Code it once; reuse the same canonical feature variable.",
    "not_bijective": "No demonstrated one-label-per-object convention; same-group scenarios retained.",
    "fine_membership": "Unresolved shared fine strokes cannot support two independent confident positive codes. Where ownership affects a feature, use unknown. Enumeration relaxes residual across-group and across-feature coupling; describe outer bounds, not sharp jointly realizable shapes."
  },
  "coder_instructions": [
    "Read the frozen complete four-feature definitions in feature_codebook_v1.json and measurement_review/review_v1.txt. Do not adjust thresholds, feature families, candidates or crop orientation based on results.",
    "For each canonical group and each feature give value 0 or 1 or null, allowed binary set, actual native view and original-image coordinate evidence, reason and uncertainty. Every positive needs a clear sufficient witness; every zero needs all relevant candidate extent inspected. Unknown is expected for missing ends, text contacts, uncertain ownership and threshold overlap.",
    "G1 and G3 need conservative width/length ranges and original-image coordinate witnesses; ranges must be visibly supported, not chosen to reach threshold. Do not claim precise segmentation or biological size. Borderline or unmeasurable stays unknown.",
    "Do not treat old envelope as a mask; possible marks cannot be silently included or removed. No drawing repair, automatic text erasure or speculative reconstruction.",
    "Record a shared canonical group once; preserve all 48 candidate-group feature opportunities and map to the nine loci. Do not compute same-label consistency during coding.",
    "Freeze the completed observation matrix and read/view receipt before root derives 36-pair tables and global contrast bounds. Record conflicting codes as a problem, not an average."
  ],
  "numerical_scope": "Only after the complete matrix freeze, apply codebook to each of the 16 full candidate scenarios; report all 36 pairs, three mixed strata, four feature contributions and T11/T00. Bounds use explicitly relaxed binary domains and are not confidence intervals. Another implementation must independently replay numbers, not re-label images as independent evidence.",
